au3 passes wxString to APIs taking (const char*) or (const wxChar*) in
several places -- TranslatableString::untranslatable() (which only
overloads on (const char*) and (const QString&)), sqlite3_exec()/
sqlite3_prepare_v2()/GetValue() (which take UTF-8 SQL strings),
SettingsVisitorBase::Define() and ExportFFmpegOptions::
FetchCompatibleCodecList() (whose key/format parameters are
const wxChar*), Nyquist cvstring() (which takes const char*), and a
(const char*) cast.  That compiles only when wxWidgets still allows
the unsafe implicit wxString conversion (wxUSE_UNSAFE_WXSTRING_CONV);
with it disabled (e.g. openSUSE wxWidgets 3.2) it is a hard error:

  error: no matching function for call to
         'TranslatableString::untranslatable(wxString&)'
  error: cannot convert 'wxString' to 'const char*'
  error: invalid cast from type 'wxString' to type 'const char*'

Route the TranslatableString arguments through the au3::untranslatable(
const wxString&) bridge from WxMuseStringCompat.h -- the same idiom
Internat.h's Verbatim(const wxString&) already uses --, convert the
sqlite3 SQL strings explicitly with .ToUTF8().data() (the idiom
ProjectFileIO.cpp already uses for sqlite3_open_v2), and pass setting
keys as static_cast<const wxChar*>(key.c_str()) (the idiom NyquistBase
already uses for the other Define() call sites).  UTF-8 round-trip
preserves non-ASCII names on every platform.  Call sites passing
(const char*), (const XML_Char*), char arrays, string literals, or
wxCharBuffer-returning .mb_str()/.fn_str()/.ToUTF8() are left untouched.

PATCH-FIX-UPSTREAM: upstream relies on wxUSE_UNSAFE_WXSTRING_CONV.

